                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <p rendition="#center">[From Official Gazette of September 19, 1914.]</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Decree concerning clergy</hi>.</p>
                <p>Office of the Secretary of the Constitutionalist Government of the Free and
                    Sovereign State of Veracruz.</p>
                <p>In order to explain the resolution made by the Governor and Military Commander of
                    the State, General Candido Aguilar, relative to the clergy, I hereby make known
                    that he has ordered the definite expulsion of the foreign clergymen, permitting
                    the nationals to exercise their functions, in the following proportions.</p>
                <p>In towns: of 500 to 10,000 inhabitants, one priest; of 10,000 to 30,000
                    inhabitants, two priests; from 30,000 upwards, up to four priests as a
                    maximum.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Jalapa</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-11">11th of September, 1914.</date>
                        Government Secretary, Heriberto Jara.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
